# UIT-FIXED Project Rules

## 1. Existing Technology Stack
- Backend: NestJS, TypeScript, Prisma 6, PostgreSQL 16.
- Frontend: React 19, Vite, TypeScript.
- File storage: Cloudinary.
- Preserve the existing project architecture and dependencies.
- Do not replace existing technologies without explicit approval.

## 2. Codebase First
- Inspect existing code before creating or modifying files.
- Reuse existing modules, utilities, services and dependencies.
- Avoid duplicate implementations.
- Follow the existing naming and coding conventions.

## 3. Business Rules
- Follow the uit-fixed-workflow Skill for all business logic.
- Never invent unconfirmed UIT buildings, departments or workflows.
- Enforce authorization on the backend.
- Do not trust role, user ID or department ID supplied by the client without verification.

## 4. Database
- Follow the database-prisma Skill.
- Preserve existing data and migration history.
- Never run destructive database commands without explicit approval.

## 5. Development Workflow
- Understand the requested task before editing.
- Inspect relevant files.
- Present an implementation plan for tasks involving multiple files.
- Keep changes scoped to the requested feature.
- Add or update tests for changed business logic.
- Run relevant tests and report their results.
- Do not claim tests passed if they were not executed.

## 6. Collaboration
- Respect existing API contracts.
- Avoid modifying unrelated files.
- Do not introduce unnecessary dependencies.
- Explain important design decisions and assumptions.